    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d245">

                <pb facs="0240" n="228" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg228"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.42/111: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Dreyfus</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-03-13T23:00:00-04:00">March 13, 1942—11
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>67. Because of transportation difficulties, the Monroe Mission<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d245-f1"/> will be unable to proceed this spring. It plans, however,
                    to make the <pb facs="0241" n="229" xml:id="pg229"/> trip next fall. Please
                    inform Iranian Government, emphasizing that this is merely a postponement, that
                    there is no intention of abandoning the undertaking, and that, as Sadiq
                    originally indicated, the fall is really preferable for the accomplishment of
                    the mission’s purpose.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d245-f1" n="2" xml:id="d245-f1-content">
                <p>Educational Mission headed by Professor Paul Monroe of Columbia University.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
